{"id": "sdqa0104", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 542423949, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "9d39a2003e15ffbac1b46fe5b0a53c242ef024ed6b8b1e37a92e22d426213d95", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 3, "query": "What is a motor tic?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0104.wav", "input_sha256": "7b3a62a04f0793fc567b2f80e5b918eeaa7453b7d88fd2a018d2a33fe8151311", "input_samples": 60752, "input_s": 3.797, "n_real_chunks": 4, "score": 0.5658, "act": 0.9969, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "A motor tic is a sudden, brief, repetitive movement that a person feels driven to do, often without full voluntary control. Examples include: Eye blinking , Facial grimacing , Shoulder shrugging , Head jerking , Nose twitching Motor tics can be simple — like blinking — or complex, involving coordinated movements such as jumping, touching objects, or making gestures. “Tick” usually refers to the insect; the medical term is tic.", "expert_answer": "A **motor tic** is a sudden, brief, repetitive movement that a person feels driven to do, often without full voluntary control.\n\nExamples include:\n\n- Eye blinking\n- Facial grimacing\n- Shoulder shrugging\n- Head jerking\n- Nose twitching\n\nMotor tics can be **simple** — like blinking — or **complex**, involving coordinated movements such as jumping, touching objects, or making gestures.\n\n“Tick” usually refers to the insect; the medical term is **tic**.", "transcript": "What is a motor tick?\n", "asr_s": 2.29, "expert_s": 2.98, "expert_input_samples": 60752, "expert_input_s": 3.797, "expert_input_sha256": "7b3a62a04f0793fc567b2f80e5b918eeaa7453b7d88fd2a018d2a33fe8151311", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 3.619, "relay_synth_ms": 15321, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_sp